@startuml code_review_layers

title Code Review Layers

note "Run all three layers in parallel as fresh focused review tasks with the same review input.\nRequire overlapping child-session execution; never fall back to sequential execution.\nComplete every step and collect all layer-related issues independently.\nDo not stop when a layer finds issues and do not pass findings between layers.\nVerify, deduplicate and report findings only after all three layers complete." as LayerNote

rectangle "1. Solution and architecture" {
  rectangle "Understand the requirement" as Requirements
  rectangle "Validate the requirement is completely implemented" as Solution
  rectangle "Validate architecture and code structure" as Architecture
  rectangle "Validate interfaces and cross-domain communication" as Interfaces
  rectangle "Collect all layer-related issues with evidence and coverage" as ArchitectureIssues
}

rectangle "2. Unit correctness" {
  rectangle "Review unit implementations, find implementation bugs and edge cases" as Units
  rectangle "Validate unit-test correctness and completeness" as Tests
  rectangle "Collect all layer-related issues with evidence and coverage" as UnitIssues
}

rectangle "3. Code polish" {
  rectangle "Review code style and formatting" as Style
  rectangle "Review minor issues (naming, etc.)" as Naming
  rectangle "Collect all layer-related issues with evidence and coverage" as PolishIssues
}

rectangle "Verify and deduplicate findings from all layers" as Consolidate
rectangle "Render one complete severity-prioritized report" as Report

Requirements --> Solution
Solution --> Architecture
Architecture --> Interfaces
Interfaces --> ArchitectureIssues

Units --> Tests
Tests --> UnitIssues

Style --> Naming
Naming --> PolishIssues

ArchitectureIssues --> Consolidate
UnitIssues --> Consolidate
PolishIssues --> Consolidate
Consolidate --> Report

@enduml
